w(E,"Camera Obscura Workshop (slides)","Education/Photography/Camera Obscura Workshop",gp('1jLoV9G4lOgPI3iUcaQLBxNZJuP-Ro6r1rHFCmJx0sFs'),'slides','2018-06-13','low',['curriculum','learning-festivals'],"Skeleton slide deck for the DIY Camera Obscura workshop (Delia Stephens and Alex Tran): five section titles only.","""
DIY CAMERA OBSCURA, Delia Stephens and Alex Tran. Sections: 1. The physics of light; 2. Building the camera; 3. The camera obscura; 4. The "rules" of photography; 5. Try it yourself. (Slides contain only titles; see the Syllabus and PDF handout for details.)
""")
w(E,"Camera Obscura (handout)","Education/Photography/Camera Obscura.pdf",gf('15Apz9O8mGY94QEbHmIlU8IdiQdmeA_SF'),'pdf','2018-05-25','medium',['curriculum','learning-festivals'],"Student handout for building a cardboard-box camera obscura with a magnifying glass lens and tracing-paper screen.","""
DIY camera obscura. Students learn what light is, how humans process light, how cameras work; at the end take an instant-camera photo and learn the chemistry of instant photography.

Materials: cardboard box, scissors, 4 popsicle sticks, tape (share with a buddy), magnifying glass, laminated tracing paper.
Steps: 1 mark the center of each small side of the box with a ruler; 2 cut a larger hole (for your eyes) at one end and a smaller one at the other (for the magnifying glass); 3 tape the magnifying glass over the small hole; 4 build a frame for the laminated paper from popsicle sticks; 5 slide the tracing paper back and forth until an inverted image is clear. Adapted from pinholephotography.org.
""")
w(E,"Syllabus (Camera Obscura)","Education/Photography/Syllabus",gd('1S14lUwUBfQ_gpx1bHfXMAeXUk5UH2_zm4W0xqE4cL5k'),'doc','2018-05-22','high',['curriculum','learning-festivals'],"Syllabus for 'Picture This': a 2-hour camera obscura workshop by Delia Stephens and Alex Tran with minute-by-minute plan and materials.","""
**Instructors:** Delia Stephens and Alex Tran. Based on pinholephotography.org camera obscura.

**Website description:** students construct a camera obscura (precursor of the camera) projecting images onto tracing paper, learning the physics of light and the chemistry of film photography.

**Plan (2 hours):** 0:00-0:30 Physics of light (what is light, how the eye works, camera obscura intro); 0:30-1:00 Build the camera (pass out boxes, cut holes, create tracing paper "cards"); 1:00-1:30 Breakdown (how a camera works, art and science of photography, what to change for better pictures); 1:30-2:00 Chemistry of an instant camera, take a picture with an instant camera.

**Materials:** cardboard boxes, scissors, tape, popsicle sticks, tracing paper (plus magnifying glasses and instant camera/film; per budget, workshop camera supplies cost $125.46).

Graphic design notes: MIT colors; header font Lemon/Milk.

Not captured: "Camera Obscura.ai" (Illustrator file) and "Worksheet" (Google Drawing) could not be read.
""")
D='education-design-building-challenges'
w(D,"3...2...1...Build! (slides)","Education/Design-Building Challenges/3...2...1...Build!",gp('1ik_s8kDYlwe0h9MNam1K-1ufGq2bEzMkP0yR1a_aHPg'),'slides','2018-05-22','medium',['curriculum','learning-festivals'],"Slide deck for the engineering design workshop with three timed team challenges: Book Balance, DOTS Tower, Egg Drop.","""
Instructors: An Jimenez and Bethany Cates. Overview: what is engineering, engineering design process, challenges. "Engineers use math and science to develop solutions to technical problems"; 200+ types of engineering.

- Challenge 1, Book Balance (10 min, 4 per group): using 8 sheets of paper, build a structure at least 6 inches off the ground that holds the most books.
- Challenge 2, DOTS Tower (30 min, groups of 4): tallest tower using only DOTS gummies and toothpicks; must stand 10 seconds.
- Challenge 3, Egg Drop (25 min, groups of 4): restricted-size device from provided materials to keep a raw large egg from breaking when dropped; egg must move freely in/out (no taping), no parachutes.
Wrap-up: discuss designs.
""")
w(D,"Syllabus (Design Challenges)","Education/Design-Building Challenges/Syllabus",gd('1OHHvboHnqggIhrVP7Rca71-PU-0c_qOLqiB4npvDWVI'),'doc','2018-05-22','high',['curriculum','learning-festivals','budget-finance'],"Syllabus for the 2-hour design challenge workshop with timings, materials master list and space needs.","""
**Instructors:** Bethany Cates and An Jimenez. Inspired by MIT hands-on learning: egg capsules, paper boats, bridges holding textbooks, with household materials.

**Total time:** 2 hours (5-minute intro, 5-minute close).
- Warm-up Book Balance: 8 sheets of paper, structure 6 in off the ground holding most books; 20 min (10 build, 10 test); computer paper, books.
- Egg Drop: capsule that prevents a raw egg cracking from heights; 50 min (25 build, 25 test); paper, straws, rubber bands, tape, toothpicks, raw eggs.
- DOTS Tower: tallest standing structure from DOTS and toothpicks; 40 min (30 build, 10 measure).

**Materials master list:** books, paper, toothpicks, straws, rubber bands, tape, raw eggs, DOTS, measuring tape.

**Special accommodations:** lots of tables/space; egg drop must happen outside. (Budget lists build-workshop supplies at $145.10.)
""")
