w(K,"Coding Workshop Brainstorming + Planning","Education/Coding Workshop/Coding Workshop Brainstorming + Planning",gd('1gSflxUgPtLu2ERHJA1SS7x5uo0-2VMCypK15wBB6B4M'),'doc','2018-05-23','medium',['curriculum','learning-festivals','lessons-learned'],"Brainstorm and 5/9 planning notes for the coding workshop: Python vs Scratch decision, laptop logistics and tutorial links.","""
**Ideas:** intro to what coding is with real-world examples; Python or Scratch depending on kids' age; Hello World, name echo, Mad Libs, choose-your-own-adventure, math functions, riddle/joke/game; careers in coding; continue learning (handouts, Scratch link to show parents).
**Materials:** computers with Python loaded, Mad Libs book.
**Open questions:** laptop internet/capabilities; charging all laptops (power strips, ask other team); getting Scratch/Python on laptops; printing handouts.
**Resources:** scratch.mit.edu/tips; Getting Started Guide (PDF); example 3-hour workshop at coweb.cc.gatech.edu/ice-gt/1258; tutorials: getStarted, music, racegame.
**5/9 meeting notes:** pictures help (projector or printed pictures); slides/pics from workshop in Chile; show CS applies to any interest (security, rockets, science); give freedom to pick tutorials; saving projects via a group account; paper handout. To do: list CS applications with pics, gather tutorials, resource handout, decide what to print, write script and practice.
""")
Cc='education-circuits-lab'
w(Cc,"Spokes Circuits Workshop","Education/Circuits Lab/Spokes Circuits Workshop",gd('1tr4oqZyTJIbMr1hKsDhL6vPQON6-6UUD04xmecCe5Xk'),'doc','2018-05-13','high',['curriculum','learning-festivals','gear','budget-finance'],"Design for the circuits workshop as a sequence of mini-projects (LED circuit, Arduino, photoresistor, voltage divider, motors, electromagnetism) with materials per project. Circuits supplies cost $404 in 2018.","""
General ideas: break the build into sub-projects each with an observable output; build on prior steps; as much hands-on as possible, little lecturing. Target audience (General Notes, circuits folder): 11 to 15 years, middle school.

- Mini 1, LED circuit: how a breadboard works; resistors in series/parallel; Ohm's law; ground and power. Materials: Arduino, wires, resistor, LED, laptop, USB cable.
- Mini 2, LED circuit 2: introduce Arduino for flexibility; blink; change on/off times in prepared code.
- Mini 3, photoresistor: add photoresistor so light level dims/brightens LEDs (covering it raises resistance, dims LED).
- Mini 4, voltage divider with photoresistor: voltage divider equation; two resistors then one photoresistor; midpoint to LED/Arduino.
- Mini 6, motor basics: fidget spinner idea.
- Mini 7, electromagnetism: 18g copper wire (precut), AA/AAA batteries, neodymium magnets.
Planned kit sources: Elegoo Arduino kit and micro servos (Amazon); MakeCrate (Delia's mother's company) offered donated electronics kits (musical instrument kit).
""")
